From f69cf481bd0c4a2dffee3d129e0302b4e027e838 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:42:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Sites: tracker logins and search pages as missing-episode
 sources

A new "Sites" page (below RSS) stores tracker sites: URLs, login fields
(passkey, rsskey, authkey, ...), session cookies and extra headers
(encrypted, write-only), search URL templates with {query}, and the
torrent-page / download link patterns (/torrent/{id}/,
/download.php?id={id}&passkey={passkey}).

- ~110 presets generated from the autobrr indexer definitions (site facts
  only: names, URLs, login fields, link templates) by
  scripts/gen-site-presets.mjs; SuperBits includes its search URLs.
- Search responses are auto-detected: JSON APIs (result list and fields
  found heuristically, or set by dot paths), HTML search pages (torrent
  links found by the page-link pattern, seeders/size from the row) and
  RSS/Torznab. "Test search" shows results, masked links and the mapping.
- Enabled sites are searched by missing-episode checks; downloads use the
  site's link with its cookies. RSS feeds and torrent links on a site's
  host carry its cookies too.
- Templates may only target the site's own hosts; cookies/headers are
  dropped on cross-host redirects; secrets are masked in test output and
  never returned by the API.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
